%T A397850 107789,18088,110432,702267,201172,951812,4665849,2011782,7929550,
%U A397850 31615313,18774656,64537420,218358547,167112026,516754214,1535560265,1438190386,4090202022,10977572595
%N A397850 Number of tilings of a 4 X n rectangle using straight trominoes and Z-tetrominoes.
%C A397850 Rotations and reflections of the pieces are allowed, so both chiralities (S and Z) of the tetromino may be used.
%C A397850 The Z-tetromino alone cannot tile any rectangle (a classical result), and straight trominoes alone cannot tile a 4 X n rectangle unless n is divisible by 3 (area argument). Hence for n not divisible by 3, every tiling uses both kinds of pieces. The smallest such n admitting a tiling is n = 11, with a(11) = 8; note the remarkably small value a(13) = 2.
%C A397850 It appears that a(n) > 0 for all n >= 11. (Empirical observation.)
%C A397850 Tilings that use both kinds of pieces are counted at the Grekov link; a(n) equals that count plus the number of tilings by straight trominoes alone, since Z-tetrominoes alone cannot tile the rectangle.
%D A397850 S. W. Golomb, Polyominoes, 2nd ed., Princeton University Press, 1994.
%H A397850 D. Grekov, <a href="https://polyominoes.org/data/3I+4Z">Tilings of rectangles by straight trominoes and Z-tetrominoes</a> (counts tilings that use both kinds of pieces).
%H A397850 Javier Alejandro Cabrera Otten, <a href="/A397850/a397850.txt">Python program (transfer matrix, terms, and recurrence certificate)</a>
%F A397850 G.f.: x^3*(3 - 6*x^2 - 23*x^3 + 3*x^4 + 31*x^5 + 55*x^6 - 29*x^7 - 65*x^8 - 51*x^9 + 87*x^10 + 66*x^11 - 3*x^12 - 93*x^13 - 28*x^14 + 34*x^15 + 38*x^16 - 21*x^18 - 3*x^19 - x^20 + 7*x^21 + 2*x^22 - x^23 - x^24 + x^26 - x^27)/(1 - 2*x^2 - 12*x^3 + x^4 + 19*x^5 + 46*x^6 - 14*x^7 - 58*x^8 - 70*x^9 + 70*x^10 + 97*x^11 + 34*x^12 - 132*x^13 - 84*x^14 + 31*x^15 + 109*x^16 + 38*x^17 - 57*x^18 - 41*x^19 - 5*x^20 + 32*x^21 + 5*x^22 - 8*x^24 - 2*x^25 + 2*x^26 - x^29 + x^30).
%F A397850 a(n) = 2*a(n-2) + 12*a(n-3) - a(n-4) - 19*a(n-5) - 46*a(n-6) + 14*a(n-7) + 58*a(n-8) + 70*a(n-9) - 70*a(n-10) - 97*a(n-11) - 34*a(n-12) + 132*a(n-13) + 84*a(n-14) - 31*a(n-15) - 109*a(n-16) - 38*a(n-17) + 57*a(n-18) + 41*a(n-19) + 5*a(n-20) - 32*a(n-21) - 5*a(n-22) + 8*a(n-24) + 2*a(n-25) - 2*a(n-26) + a(n-29) - a(n-30) for n > 30.
%e A397850 For n = 3 the a(3) = 3 tilings use straight trominoes only: four horizontal trominoes; or three vertical trominoes covering the top three rows and one horizontal tromino in the bottom row; or the vertical reflection of the latter.
